{# PERFORMANCE · CONFIGURE — what this section opens on, and the rules the
   figures on it are read under.

   READ-ONLY, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN, exactly as the departments section's
   settings are. The window and the comparison are chosen in the HEADER, on
   the page they are about, and that choice is in the address so it can be
   sent to somebody; a second control here would be a second place the same
   decision lived.

   WHAT IT IS FOR: the rules. A reader who wants to know why a cell is shaded,
   or why a department has no figure, finds the answer here rather than in the
   code — and the numbers that state those rules are read from the one place
   that holds them, never typed twice.

   THE STRIP ABOVE IS THIS SURFACE'S SECTIONS, written by the shell's frame. #}
{% extends '@Shell/page.html.twig' %}

{% block title %}Performance{% endblock %}

{% block stylesheets %}
    {{ parent() }}
    {{ include('@Team/performance/_stylesheets.html.twig') }}
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_breadcrumbs %}
    <a href="{{ path('team_index') }}">uhifadhi</a> /
    <a href="{{ path('team_departments') }}">departments</a> /
    <a href="{{ path('team_performance') }}">performance</a> / configure
{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page_title %}Performance{% endblock %}
{% block shell_page_subtitle %}What this section opens on, and what a period is read against.{% endblock %}

{% block shell_page %}
    <div class="grid g2">
        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">The reading<span class="src">&middot; what a page opens on</span></span>
            <div class="rln"><span>Window on open</span><span class="mono d">{{ kinds|first }}</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Windows offered</span><span class="mono d">{{ kinds|join(' · ')|lower }}</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Compared with, on open</span><span class="mono d">{{ comparisons|first }}</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Comparisons offered</span><span class="mono d">{{ comparisons|length }}</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Where the choice lives</span><span class="mono d">the address, so a page can be sent to somebody</span></div>
        </div>

        <div class="c">
            <span class="tab">The shades<span class="src">&middot; what a tint claims</span></span>
            <div class="rln"><span>What a shade is</span><span class="mono d">a placing inside one column and one band</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>A column with no polarity</span><span class="mono d">never tinted</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>Fewest figures to place a column</span><span class="mono d">{{ fewest }}</span></div>
            <div class="rln"><span>An absence</span><span class="mono d">dashed, and never a pale figure</span></div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="zone">The topics this installation carries</h2>

    <div class="c">
        <span class="tab">Topics<span class="src">&middot; the host's own, then a module's in the order the organization arranged them</span></span>
        {% for topic in topics %}
            <div class="rln">
                <span>{{ topic.title }}</span>
                <span class="mono d">{{ topic.publisher }}</span>
            </div>
        {% else %}
            <p class="perf-empty">This installation publishes no topics at all, which is not the same as an organization with nothing to report.</p>
        {% endfor %}
    </div>
{% endblock %}
